
Iceberg data is taken from - BYU Antarctic Iceberg Tracking Database (1978–present, satellite scatterometer): https://www.scp.byu.edu/data/iceberg/database1.html
        the consolidated database data and statistical database data were downlaoded and merged into 1 file - tracks.csv by using make_tracks.py

Wind and sea surface temperature data was taken from https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/ from the dataset page - "ERA5 hourly data on single levels from 1940 to present"
        here data only for the year 2019 has been taken. data for more years can be taken for better modle training 
        file named as - era5_2019.nc
Current and sea ice data was taken from - https://data.marine.copernicus.eu/product/GLOBAL_MULTIYEAR_PHY_001_030/description  .   again data for the year 2019 has been taken
        file named as - glorys_2019.nc

All these 3 files-[ tracks.csv, era5_2019.nc, glorys_2019.nc ] were merged into 1 file - training_data.csv - using build_dataset.py
